From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:37:16 -0400
Subject: fix: pinned rows stay above the line while a drag is over a folder
 (issue 33)

pins H14 (docs/features/pins.md), GitHub issue 33. When a loose tab's row
was dragged in among the Space's pins and the pointer moved over a folder's
header, the folder took the drag and the sidebar list reset its drag state.
The list's next layout judged the dragged row by its own pin, which is a
loose tab's, so the Clear line was drawn above the row and every pinned
folder and pin after it slid under the line until the pointer left the
header.

The list's layout now keeps the side the dragged rows had for as long as
the drag goes on, also while another target holds it. It finds those rows
through the drag handler, and between the run's last row and the first loose
row it keeps the side last drawn. The drag handler lays the list out again
whenever a drag ends (DestroyDragController), so a release, Esc or a lost
capture over a folder draws the line from the tabs' pins again.

Test: PinnedRunTest.PinnedRowsStayAboveTheLineWhileADragIsOverAFolder.

Why: the line, the pins and the pinned folders jumped under the line during an ordinary drag into the pinned run.
Removable when: the sidebar list keeps its drag state while a folder target holds the drag, or the folder target stops resetting it.
---
 .../ui/views/tabs/common/tab_drag_handler.cc  |  12 +
 .../unpinned_tab_container_view_layout.cc     |  29 +-
 .../test/stedding/pinned_run_browsertest.cc   | 254 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 290 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/common/tab_drag_handler.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/common/tab_drag_handler.cc
index d597168b26a02..22cb636c57240 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/common/tab_drag_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/common/tab_drag_handler.cc
@@ -1255,6 +1255,18 @@ std::unique_ptr<TabDragController> TabDragHandlerImpl::ReleaseDragController() {
 void TabDragHandlerImpl::DestroyDragController() {
   drag_controller_.reset();
   stedding_press_drag::ReleaseHeldPage(&tab_strip_region_view_.get());
+  // pins H14 (GitHub issue 33): while another target, a folder's header or
+  // rows, holds the drag, the list draws its dragged rows on the side of the
+  // Clear line they were last drawn on, and nothing tells the list when such
+  // a drag ends: the release, Esc or a lost capture goes to that target.
+  // Every drag ends here, so the list draws the line by the tabs' pins again.
+  if (auto* const strip = views::AsViewClass<TabStripView>(
+          tab_strip_region_view_->GetTabStripView())) {
+    if (UnpinnedTabContainerView* const list =
+            strip->GetUnpinnedTabsContainer()) {
+      list->InvalidateLayout();
+    }
+  }
 }
 
 void TabDragHandlerImpl::StartedDragging(
